1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,340
Thirty-four dollars quietly disappears from your checking account every single month.

2
00:00:04,230 --> 00:00:07,820
Holding ten thousand in checking pays point zero one percent.

3
00:00:07,870 --> 00:00:11,470
Your bank lends that cash overnight at five percent spread.

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:14,480
Pause. How much cash are you holding right now?

5
00:00:14,830 --> 00:00:17,760
Comment your idle checking balance if you dare.

6
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:22,080
Keep five thousand max in checking, sweep the rest to high yield.

7
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:25,710
High yield pays four point five, checking pays practically zero.

8
00:00:25,770 --> 00:00:29,370
Banks profit four hundred twelve dollars on your default laziness.

9
00:00:29,410 --> 00:00:32,440
Which is why thirty-four dollars quietly disappears.
